# CMake build directories
build*/
cmake-build-*/
install*/
# results*/

# Conan-generated CMake presets (local paths, regenerated every build)
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Object files
*.o
*.obj

# Executables
*.exe

# Fuzzing (see FUZZING.md) - none of this is meant to be committed:
# the harness binaries built locally (`clang++ ... -o fuzz_http_parser`
# per FUZZING.md's instructions produces a bare, extension-less
# executable at repo root on Linux/macOS - *.exe above only covers
# Windows), and anything libFuzzer writes when it actually finds
# something or is given a corpus directory to persist to. Anchored to
# root with a trailing underscore so this can never match fuzz/ (the
# source directory) itself, only fuzz_<name> binaries next to it -
# forward-compatible with harnesses added after this one.
/fuzz_*
crash-*
oom-*
timeout-*
leak-*
slow-unit-*
corpus/

# Debug symbols
*.pdb

# Static / shared libraries
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dll

# Coverage files
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov
coverage.info
coverage.filtered.info
coverage-html/

# Doxygen (fetched theme + generated output, not committed)
docs/doxygen-awesome-css/
docs/html/

# Clang tools
.clangd/
.cache/

# IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Release tarballs (downloaded locally for hash verification)
*.tar.gz